    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is the Herman Miller Aeron better than the Steelcase Gesture?</h3>
    <p>The Aeron is better for warm environments and people who want a breathable, suspended mesh seat with iconic design and a 12-year warranty. The Gesture is better for people who change posture often and move between phones, tablets, and laptops, because its 360-degree armrests track your arms through nearly any position. There is no universal winner; the right choice depends on your body, work habits, and budget.</p>

    <h3>Which chair is better for back pain, the Aeron or the Gesture?</h3>
    <p>The Aeron with PostureFit SL is the stronger choice for lower-back pain because it stabilizes the pelvis and supports the lumbar curve directly. The Gesture's live back adjusts to your spine as you recline, which helps people who shift positions throughout the day, but its lumbar support is less targeted than the Aeron's PostureFit. If back pain is your primary concern, the Aeron is the safer bet.</p>

    <h3>Is the Herman Miller Aeron worth the higher price over the Steelcase Gesture?</h3>
    <p>If breathability, premium build, and long-term resale value matter most, the Aeron's $1,495 price is justified by its 12-year warranty and durability. If budget and armrest flexibility matter more, the Gesture at $979 delivers comparable ergonomics for about $500 less. Both are excellent 10-plus-year investments that work out to roughly $80 to $125 per year of use.</p>

    <h3>Which chair is better for multi-device work?</h3>
    <p>The Steelcase Gesture wins for multi-device work because its 360-degree armrests adjust in height, width, pivot, and rotation, supporting your arms while typing, holding a phone, or using a tablet. The Aeron's armrests are adjustable but less flexible, making the Gesture the better choice for users who constantly switch between devices and postures.</p>

    <h3>Do both chairs come with a warranty?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both chairs come with a 12-year warranty that covers nearly every component, including the frame, mechanism, and casters. The Steelcase Gesture also offers a lifetime warranty in North America. Both warranties are among the best in the ergonomic chair category and reflect the build quality expected from premium task chairs.</p>

    <h3>Can I try the Herman Miller Aeron or Steelcase Gesture before buying?</h3>
    <p>Yes, both chairs are available for testing at authorized dealers and many premium office furniture showrooms. Herman Miller and Steelcase both have dealer networks where you can sit in multiple size and configuration options. Some online retailers also offer 30-day return policies, but testing in person is recommended because the Aeron's three sizes and the Gesture's fit feel different for each body type.</p>

